      Phase-15: the Home progress ribbon (NAV-01/PERS-03/CHAL-05, D-03/D-03c/D-03h;
      ux-spec §4.2, §8).

      `stat_value_unknown` is an em dash, and it is what a pill shows both before the first
      read lands AND when the read failed — the two are deliberately indistinguishable, and
      neither is ever rendered as `0`, because zero is a real answer for a brand-new player
      and reporting it for a broken read would lie to an experienced one (D-03h).
      `stat_value_unknown_desc` is what a screen reader says in its place, so the em dash is
      never spoken as punctuation.

      The Boards pill's denominator is a FORMAT ARGUMENT, never a literal: it is supplied at
      the call site from the Classic catalogue's own size, so a stored row cannot change a
      shipped number and a sixth board would move it without a copy edit.
    -->
