      shown to a signed-in player ONLY. Signed out, they are absent rather than disabled:
      a greyed-out "Leaderboards" is an affordance that explains nothing, whereas the
      sign-in row directly above it already says what to do. While the session is still
      Unknown the whole section is absent (Phase 11 D-11), these rows included.

      Both labels are fixed verbatim by D-14. "Leaderboards" is plural because the row
      opens the all-leaderboards picker, not one board — the supporting lines describe
      looking at what is already there, since neither row submits anything. No id and no
      player-identifying text belongs in either: the seam takes no argument for these.
