    <!-- ====================== Phase-13 cloud-save copy ====================== -->
    <!--
      CLOUD-03 / D-11 — the ONE line the player reads under this game's entry in the
      Play Games saved-games list. It is written into the snapshot's metadata at commit
      time and therefore follows the DEVICE LOCALE AT THAT MOMENT, by design: a player
      who changes language sees the new language on their next solve rather than a line
      frozen in whatever locale first wrote the save. That is why the numbers cross the
      platform seam as three raw ints (CloudSaveDescription) and the wording lives only
      here, where a translator can reach it.

      Four positional arguments, in order: the Challenge ladder level, total stars,
      Classic boards cleared, and the size of the Classic roster. The fourth is supplied
      from ClassicBoard.entries.size and is NOT a literal 5 anywhere — a sixth Classic
      board must move this denominator on its own.

      Positional %1$d-style arguments throughout, matching settings_play_games_signed_in_as;
      a bare %d would be untranslatable the moment a language needs another word order.
      The separator is a middle dot rather than a comma so the three figures read as
      peers rather than as a sentence.
    -->
    <string name="cloud_save_description">Meydan okuma seviyesi %1$d · %2$d yıldız · %3$d/%4$d Klasik tahta</string>

    <!--
      D-12 to D-15 — the ONE dialog the v1.1 requirements reserved. Every other conflict
      in this phase resolves silently by monotonic merge (CLOUD-02); this one cannot,
      because merging two different players' progress is not a merge, it is a leak.

      The body is a wipe list, not a warning. D-14 requires the copy to state exactly what
      "Use their cloud progress" replaces, so it names all four categories the replace path
      deletes: level results, play history, the Challenge level, and both in-progress
      games. Any later edit that shortens this sentence must keep all four — a player who
      could not have known what they were authorising is the failure this copy exists to
      prevent.

      Two bodies, one wording. profile_swap_body names the arriving account through a
      positional %1$s; profile_swap_body_unknown_account is the fallback for a display name
      the SDK could not look up (Phase 11 D-14), which is a degraded name and never a
      failed sign-in — so it says "this account" rather than leaving a gap or rendering the
      word null.

      The two labels are account-neutral on purpose. "Keep this device's progress" is the
      safe answer and carries the gradient CTA; "Use their cloud progress" is the
      destructive one and is a plain text button. The arriving account is named in the
      body, where both variants have room, rather than in a label that would need a sixth
      string to stay readable when the name is unknown.
    -->
    <string name="profile_swap_title">Farklı bir hesaba mı geçiyorsun?</string>
    <string name="profile_swap_body">%1$s olarak oturum açtın. Bu cihazın ilerlemesini korumak, onu bu hesabın bulut kaydıyla birleştirir — iki tarafta da hiçbir şey kaybolmaz. Bunun yerine bu hesabın bulut ilerlemesini kullanmak, bu cihazdaki her şeyin yerine geçer: seviye sonuçların, oyun geçmişin, Meydan okuma seviyen ve devam eden iki oyunun.</string>
    <string name="profile_swap_body_unknown_account">Farklı bir Play Games hesabıyla oturum açtın. Bu cihazın ilerlemesini korumak, onu bu hesabın bulut kaydıyla birleştirir — iki tarafta da hiçbir şey kaybolmaz. Bunun yerine bu hesabın bulut ilerlemesini kullanmak, bu cihazdaki her şeyin yerine geçer: seviye sonuçların, oyun geçmişin, Meydan okuma seviyen ve devam eden iki oyunun.</string>
    <string name="profile_swap_keep">Bu cihazın ilerlemesini koru</string>
    <string name="profile_swap_use_cloud">Bulut ilerlemesini kullan</string>
